        "current": "\nThe canonical ETH/OMR market is the current market model. Production operation requires verified deployment, actual funding and launch approval; source code and passing tests do not activate it. The production token rail remains inactive.\n\nThe restricted settlement manager collects a fixed 3.5% base fee on buys and sells: 1.27% to the developer recipient, 0.51% to RWA, 0.76% to the community and 0.96% to protocol-owned liquidity, with rounding remainder assigned to POL. A separate 0.5% allocation funds WBTC holder rewards, making the ordinary protocol charge 4%. The Hook adds a sell-pressure surcharge capped at 0.5%, for a maximum protocol charge of 4.5%, without collecting the base or rewards again. LP fees and network gas are additional. The planned genesis pool uses a separate static 0.3% LP fee; its opening buy charges and caps are disabled. Base rates, allocation shares and recipients are fixed for the deployment; there is no Committee or Safe fee-change queue. Exact-input swaps pay in actual output (OMR on buys, ETH on sells); exact-output swaps pay in actual input (ETH on buys, OMR on sells). Partial fills use settled deltas, so effective rates on the amount a user specifies can differ. Every ETH/OMR swap admitted by this manager pays the base and WBTC rewards allocation, including pools without a Hook. Independent third-party receipts, custody arrangements and venues fall outside this policy's guarantees.\n\nCore liquidity and the War Chest have separate budgets. Controllers enforce finite action, episode and lifetime capacity. Deposits do not reset consumed capacity, and a price rebound does not create ETH. Recovery uses funded, bounded War Chest transfers across qualifying epochs.\n\n",
