        "current": "    <p>One five-day ETH/OMR auction on Robinhood Chain is open to character NFT holders once launch verification clears. Paid and free-credit NFTs qualify, with no individual allocation caps. The target is around noon New York on October 9–14, 2026; verified native block boundaries determine the window, so exact wall-clock timing is not guaranteed.</p>\n    <p>The 100M OMR allocation is 40M for the sale, 20M for initial liquidity and 40M retained in the Safe for later bond activation. Unsold auction tokens return to the Safe and are accounted separately. The successful-raise minimum is 10 ETH, with a starting floor corresponding approximately to 10 ETH for all 40M offered tokens.</p>\n    <p>50% of accepted ETH funds liquidity with the 20M token allocation, subject to tightly bounded rounding. The pool's opening price follows these funded amounts independently of the final auction price and can be lower. All remaining accepted ETH goes to the Safe's Family Yield treasury; this does not activate game reward conversion or payouts. After successful closure, exit your bid and claim filled tokens without waiting for LP migration. Completed purchases are final; unused bid ETH is returned.</p>\n    <p>The current source configures a fixed 3.5% base fee on buys and sells, split 1.27% developer, 0.51% RWA, 0.76% community and 0.96% POL, with rounding remainder assigned to POL. A separate 0.5% allocation funds WBTC holder rewards, making the ordinary protocol charge 4%. A sell-pressure surcharge is capped at 0.5%, for a maximum protocol charge of 4.5%; LP fees and network gas are additional. The restricted manager collects the base and rewards; the Hook avoids collecting them twice. The planned genesis pool uses a separate static 0.3% LP fee, with opening buy charges and caps disabled. Deployed rates and recipients are fixed; there is no Committee or Safe fee-change queue. Production trading remains inactive and requires verified deployment, sealed-token funding and launch approval. Read the <a href=\"/wiki#genesis\">auction terms</a> and <a href=\"/wiki#committee-tax\">fixed fee policy</a>; <a href=\"/\">check your wallet's live sale status</a> before bidding.</p>\n  </section>\n\n  <div class=\"snapshot-bar\">\n",
